            "review_text": "Richard\nLa Puente, California3846 contributions\n1\nBuffet Breakfast in the Tourist Area\nMar 2014 • Couples\nHanoi Golden Hotel Restaurant Review\n107 Nguyen Thien Thuat Street, Nha Trang\nTel: 0583-529-123\n\nGPS Coordinates: N 12º14’ 02.2”, E 109º 11’ 40.9”\n\nThis is a review of only the hotel’s 3rd floor restaurant, which is open to the general public, at least during breakfast. This is NOT a review of the hotel. The hotel's restaurant is located on the third floor of the hotel, which also located in the heart of the tourist area.\n\nWe went there chiefly because our hotel around the corner did not provide breakfast with the room. There are many venues in the area that serve everything from a simple bowl of congee or pho to elaborate buffet spreads. The Hanoi Golden (not to be confused with the Hanoi Golden 2 to the north or Golden Beach next door to the south) serves a buffet breakfast that offers good value for everyone in your party. Adult price is 100,000d and children 60,000d, which in these times is good value when you consider the selection of foods available for the price. Everyone gets to eat what they want.\n\nWe ate breakfast here several times during our stay in Nha Trang. The food is very good and the selections are numerous. There is a pho station, egg station, and pancake station. All of the stations deliver food quickly and efficiently. In front of the pho and eggs stations, there are bowls of condiments for everything, including chilies and sauces.\n\nHere are some of the foods served at the inclusive buffet breakfast. Some foods alternated on different days, like soups, curry, fruits, etc., and probably market dependent.\n\nRice congee\nSeaweed soup\nShrimp cream soup\nPho - beef\nSalted egg\nStewed beef with mushroom \nStewed pork\nBacon\nPancakes\nSausage\nFried rice\nChow main\nFish stomach with vegetables\nEgg rolls\nRoasted chicken with vegetables\nStir fried noodles with shrimp\nStir fried vegetables\nStir fried bean sprouts\nStir fried yams\n\nFruits, like:\nPineapple \nWatermelon\nPassion fruit\nBanana \nRambutan \nLongans\nGuava\nMango \nTangerine\nSmall green apple\nPomelo \n\nOkra\nProcessed meats, like ham and pork\nFruit salad jello\nLettuce \nSliced Tomatoes\nSliced cucumbers\nSliced carrots\nColeslaw \nCheeses\n\nSliced bread\nBaguettes\nStrawberry jam\nOrange jam (marmalade)\nSmall pastries \n\nHot water\nLipton tea\nCoffee with or without condensed milk\n\nWatermelon juice \nOrange juice\nPineapple juice (fresh on the day I tried it)\nGreen tea (cold not hot)\n\nCatsup\nFish sauce\nSoy sauce\nChili sauce\nChilies\nLemon slices\n\nFor a person that enjoys breakfast as their biggest meal of the day, you cannot beat this venue for variety and price. The F&B manager’s name is Thieu. He’s hard working, helpful and genuinely friendly.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten March 3, 2014",
            "rating": 5.0,
